\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. With you, I will tarry, Jesus
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And I shall serve only you.
\par Never shall I be scared a-way
\par I shall follow your good ways.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par You are the goodness of my life.
\par The gloriousness of my life.
\par As the vine gives life to its boughs,
\par So shall you  give unto me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Who is it that grant me goodness,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Than you, generous donor?
\par Bounteous goodness abound in you
\par For me who's always in need.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is it that gives me comfort
\par More than you, my goodly Lord
\par Into whose hands have been ve-sted
\par Pow'r  in heaven and on earth.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. Where shall such a lord be sighted
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Who has done as Jesus did?
\par He has by His blood purchased me
\par From the powers of sin and death.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Shall not I belong unto Him
\par Who has changed His life for death?
\par shall I have to make a promise
\par That I'll ever follow Him?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  In my joys, in my agony
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 I shall stay by you each day.
\par I surrender soul and body
\par And my spirit unto you.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I shall do just as you wish me
\par If you bid me leave, I'll go.
\par If I stay by your side daily
\par I can even die with ease.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   Be with me in this earthly life
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 and when'er my end draws nearer;
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0\qj When the day doth draweth closer;
\par And the gloom of death draws nigh;
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0\qj There and then lay Thine hands on me;
\par Bless Thou me and say to me;
\par See, my child, thy life on earth ended
\par and so come and stay with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   6.   When death takes to frightening me,
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 Jesus, Lord, stand by my side.
\par Be my light in deaths dark valley
\par grant me all eternal light!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When my sight is getting gloomy,
\par Be the source of light for me;
\par That from here I shall go thither
\par \pard       As a stranger to his home.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

